            <div xml:id="d46">

                <pb facs="0159" n="47" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg47"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 9786.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Wilson to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-10-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 9, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 627.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    duplicate copies, together with translation of same, of a convention between the
                    Argentine Republic and the oriental Republic of Uruguay, providing for the
                    suppression of the authentication of signatures in requisitorial letters between
                    the courts of the two countries. The exchange of ratifications of the convention
                    took place on the 4th instant.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>




